IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `da-claims`

-- Defamation Act 2005 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters,
-- over the baseline's rules in da-claims.l4 (with the Limitation Act 2005 ss 15, 40 it uses).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES (type `Role`):
--   * `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` -- the baseline's seat: the person defamed (the aggrieved person),
--     or someone whose company or late relative was the subject;
--   * `I published something that someone says defames them` -- new: the publisher, to whom Part 3 speaks ("The publisher
--     may make an offer", ss 13-18) and against whom the defences (ss 25-33) and the damages (ss 35, 37) run.
-- The court and the Minister are never a seat; what they may do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything
-- else. The questions of one situation share one input, the same name, type and @desc:
--   * person defamed: `whose reputation the matter is about` (`Whose reputation`, the baseline's): the s 9(2) question
--     arises only for `my company's`; "May I sue" takes it as an ordinary input. `I have sent the publisher a notice about
--     the matter` (s 14: two questions). `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends` (ss 14-18: four questions);
--   * publisher: `who the matter is about` (`Who the matter is about`): the s 9(2) question arises only for a company;
--     "Can they sue me" takes it as an ordinary input. `I have been sent a notice about the matter` (s 14: two questions).
--     `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends` (ss 14-18: four questions).
-- The time to sue, the defences and the damages arise in every situation of each role, and take none.
--
-- Every helper here that reads a situation enumeration lists every value with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- The rules are the baseline's; this module builds its records from plain answers and calls its functions, restating
-- none. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md,
-- "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Defamation Act 2005 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so`
    `I published something that someone says defames them`

-- The publisher's view of whose reputation the matter is about (mapped onto the baseline's `Whose reputation`).
DECLARE `Who the matter is about` IS ONE OF
    `a living person`
    `a company`
    `a person who has died`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Whether there is a claim` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `yes: there is a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)`
    `yes, but only with the leave of the court, the publisher having been sued over this matter before (s 23)`
    `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication cannot sue (s 9(1))`
    `no: there is no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))`
    `no: there is no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))`
    `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)`

DECLARE `The time to sue` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)`
    `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))`

DECLARE `What the notice does` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before suing`
    `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before suing`

DECLARE `If the offer is accepted` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the person defamed can no longer sue the publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))`
    `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))`
    `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)`

DECLARE `Which defence` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)`
    `contextual truth (s 26)`
    `honest opinion (s 31(1))`
    `triviality (s 33)`
    `none of these defences`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs, and mapping its answers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employees` IS A NUMBER
      `related` IS A BOOLEAN
      `public body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The corporation at the time of publication`
`the company from` `for profit` `employees` `related` `public body` MEANS
    `The corporation at the time of publication` WITH
        `its objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` IS `for profit`
        `the number of full-time-equivalent employees` IS `employees`
        `it is related to another corporation (Corporations Act s 50)` IS `related`
        `it is a public body` IS `public body`

GIVEN `whose` IS A `Whose reputation`
      `defamatory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company` IS A `The corporation at the time of publication`
      `publisher died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sued before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The publication`
`the publication from` `whose` `defamatory` `the company` `publisher died` `sued before` `leave` MEANS
    `The publication` WITH
        `whose reputation the matter is about` IS `whose`
        `the matter carries a defamatory imputation about them` IS `defamatory`
        `the company` IS `the company`
        `the publisher has died since publishing it` IS `publisher died`
        `I have already sued this publisher for damages over this or like matter` IS `sued before`
        `the court has given leave for the further proceedings` IS `leave`

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `names the imputations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `further particulars asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days taken` IS A NUMBER
      `extra days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My notice to the publisher`
`the notice from` `in writing` `names the imputations` `further particulars asked` `days taken` `extra days` MEANS
    `My notice to the publisher` WITH
        `it is in writing` IS `in writing`
        `it tells the publisher the defamatory imputations I say it carries about me` IS `names the imputations`
        `the publisher gave me a further particulars notice` IS `further particulars asked`
        `days I took to give the further particulars` IS `days taken`
        `extra days the publisher agreed to` IS `extra days`

GIVEN `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days to offer` IS A NUMBER
      `defence served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from withdrawal` IS A NUMBER
      `agreed days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The timing of the offer`
`the timing from` `notice given` `days to offer` `defence served` `renewal` `genuine` `days from withdrawal` `agreed days` MEANS
    `The timing of the offer` WITH
        `I gave the publisher a concerns notice` IS `notice given`
        `days from my concerns notice to the offer` IS `days to offer`
        `the publisher had served a defence in my action before the offer` IS `defence served`
        `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS `renewal`
        `it is a genuine attempt to meet my concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS `genuine`
        `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS `days from withdrawal`
        `days for renewal agreed with me beyond 14` IS `agreed days`

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `states the limit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `correction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given to others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `tells others` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The offer`
`the offer from` `in writing` `identifiable` `limited` `states the limit` `correction` `given to others` `tells others` `expenses` MEANS
    `The offer` WITH
        `it is in writing` IS `in writing`
        `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS `identifiable`
        `it is limited to particular imputations` IS `limited`
        `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS `states the limit`
        `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS `correction`
        `the publisher gave the material to others` IS `given to others`
        `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS `tells others`
        `it offers to pay my reasonable expenses before and in considering it` IS `expenses`

GIVEN `imputations true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `context true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no further harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not honestly held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `harm unlikely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The court's findings on the defences`
`the findings from` `imputations true` `context true` `no further harm` `opinion` `public interest` `proper material` `not honestly held` `harm unlikely` MEANS
    `The court's findings on the defences` WITH
        `the imputations I complain of are substantially true` IS `imputations true`
        `other imputations in the matter are substantially true` IS `context true`
        `my imputations do no further harm because of those` IS `no further harm`
        `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact` IS `opinion`
        `the opinion related to a matter of public interest` IS `public interest`
        `the opinion is based on proper material` IS `proper material`
        `I prove the publisher did not honestly hold the opinion` IS `not honestly held`
        `I was unlikely to sustain any harm in the circumstances of publication` IS `harm unlikely`

GIVEN `economic` IS A NUMBER
      `non-economic` IS A NUMBER
      `exemplary` IS A NUMBER
      `aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The court's assessment`
`the assessment from` `economic` `non-economic` `exemplary` `aggravated` MEANS
    `The court's assessment` WITH
        `damages assessed for my economic loss` IS `economic`
        `damages assessed for my non-economic loss` IS `non-economic`
        `exemplary or punitive damages sought` IS `exemplary`
        `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted` IS `aggravated`

-- Every value listed, no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who the matter is about`
GIVETH A `Whose reputation`
`the baseline's whose reputation for` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a living person` THEN `mine, and I am alive`
    WHEN `a company` THEN `my company's`
    WHEN `a person who has died` THEN `a person who has died (I would sue as family or personal representative)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Whether I may sue`
GIVETH A `Whether there is a claim`
`the claim answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `yes: a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)` THEN `yes: there is a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)`
    WHEN `yes, but only with the leave of the court, having sued this publisher over this matter before (s 23)` THEN `yes, but only with the leave of the court, the publisher having been sued over this matter before (s 23)`
    WHEN `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication (s 9(1))` THEN `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication cannot sue (s 9(1))`
    WHEN `no: no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))` THEN `no: there is no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))`
    WHEN `no: no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))` THEN `no: there is no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))`
    WHEN `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)` THEN `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `My time to sue`
GIVETH A `The time to sue`
`the time answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)` THEN `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)`
    WHEN `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))` THEN `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    WHEN `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))` THEN `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    WHEN `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))` THEN `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What my notice does`
GIVETH A `What the notice does`
`the notice answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before I sue` THEN `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before suing`
    WHEN `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before I sue` THEN `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before suing`

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `If I accept`
GIVETH AN `If the offer is accepted`
`the acceptance answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `I can no longer sue this publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))` THEN `the person defamed can no longer sue the publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))`
    WHEN `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))` THEN `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))`
    WHEN `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)` THEN `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `The defence that defeats me`
GIVETH A `Which defence`
`the defence answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)` THEN `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)`
    WHEN `contextual truth (s 26)` THEN `contextual truth (s 26)`
    WHEN `honest opinion (s 31(1))` THEN `honest opinion (s 31(1))`
    WHEN `triviality (s 33)` THEN `triviality (s 33)`
    WHEN `none of these defences` THEN `none of these defences`

§§ `The situations a question arises in`

GIVEN `whose reputation the matter is about` IS A `Whose reputation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is about my company` IF
    CONSIDER `whose reputation the matter is about`
    WHEN `mine, and I am alive` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my company's` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who has died (I would sue as family or personal representative)` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `who the matter is about` IS A `Who the matter is about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is about a company` IF
    CONSIDER `who the matter is about`
    WHEN `a living person` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who has died` THEN FALSE

§§ `For the person defamed`

§§§ `ss 7-10, 23; Limitation Act ss 15, 40 -- may I sue, and by when`

@export The matter is about my company: is it an "excluded corporation", one that may sue: a not-for-profit, or a company with fewer than 10 full-time-equivalent employees not related to another, and not a public body (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 9(2)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `whose reputation the matter is about` IS A `Whose reputation` @desc Whose reputation the matter is about: yours (and you are alive), your company's, or that of a person who has died
      `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the objects for which the company is formed include obtaining financial gain for its members (that is, it is for profit)
      `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the company employed when the matter was published, counting part-timers as fractions of a full-time equivalent
      `the company is related to another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is related to another corporation (Corporations Act 2001 s 50: a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary)
      `the company is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is a local government body or other governmental or public authority
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my company sue for defamation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `it is about my company` `whose reputation the matter is about`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my company an excluded corporation` (`the company from` `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` `the company is related to another corporation` `the company is a public body`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I, or my company, sue for defamation over this publication: no loss need be shown, but not over a person who has died, nor against a publisher who has died (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 7-10, 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `whose reputation the matter is about` IS A `Whose reputation` @desc Whose reputation the matter is about: yours (and you are alive), your company's, or that of a person who has died
      `the matter carries a defamatory imputation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter carries an imputation that is defamatory of the person or company it is about (the general law decides what is defamatory)
      `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the objects for which the company is formed include obtaining financial gain for its members (that is, it is for profit)
      `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the company employed when the matter was published, counting part-timers as fractions of a full-time equivalent
      `the company is related to another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is related to another corporation (Corporations Act 2001 s 50: a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary)
      `the company is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is a local government body or other governmental or public authority
      `the publisher has died since publishing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has died since publishing the matter
      `the publisher has already been sued for damages over this or like matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed has already sued this publisher for damages over this matter, or like matter
      `the court has given leave for the further proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave for the further proceedings (s 23)
GIVETH A `Whether there is a claim`
`Can I sue over this publication` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN `the claim answer` (`May I sue for defamation` (`the publication from` `whose reputation the matter is about` `the matter carries a defamatory imputation` (`the company from` `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` `the company is related to another corporation` `the company is a public body`) `the publisher has died since publishing it` `the publisher has already been sued for damages over this or like matter` `the court has given leave for the further proceedings`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I still in time to sue for defamation: one year from publication, or up to 3 if the court extends it (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 15, 40)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `full months since publication` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since the matter was published
      `the court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already extended the time to sue under Limitation Act s 40
GIVETH A `The time to sue`
`Is there still time for me to sue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN `the time answer` (`Am I in time to sue` `full months since publication` `the court has extended the time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 14 -- my concerns notice`

@export I have sent the publisher a notice: is it a "concerns notice", in writing and naming the imputations, with any further particulars given within 14 days (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 14(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have sent the publisher a notice about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sent or given the publisher a notice (a letter, an email, a message) about the matter
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is in writing
      `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice tells the publisher the defamatory imputations the person defamed says the matter carries about them
      `the publisher asked for further particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher gave a further particulars notice, asking for more detail of the imputations
      `days taken to give the further particulars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days were taken to give them (a large number if they were never given)
      `extra days the publisher agreed to` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 the publisher agreed to for the further particulars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my notice to the publisher a concerns notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `I have sent the publisher a notice about the matter`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my notice a concerns notice` (`the notice from` `the notice is in writing` `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` `the publisher asked for further particulars` `days taken to give the further particulars` `extra days the publisher agreed to`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have sent the publisher a notice: what does it do, and must I give one before suing (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 14; this edition has no notice precondition)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have sent the publisher a notice about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sent or given the publisher a notice (a letter, an email, a message) about the matter
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is in writing
      `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice tells the publisher the defamatory imputations the person defamed says the matter carries about them
      `the publisher asked for further particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher gave a further particulars notice, asking for more detail of the imputations
      `days taken to give the further particulars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days were taken to give them (a large number if they were never given)
      `extra days the publisher agreed to` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 the publisher agreed to for the further particulars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `What the notice does`
`What does my notice to the publisher do` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `I have sent the publisher a notice about the matter`
        THEN `the notice answer` (`What does my notice do` (`the notice from` `the notice is in writing` `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` `the publisher asked for further particulars` `days taken to give the further particulars` `extra days the publisher agreed to`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14-18 -- the publisher's offer to make amends`

@export The publisher has made me an offer to make amends: was it made in time, within 28 days of my concerns notice and before a defence was served (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 14(1), 16(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has made you an offer to make amends for the matter
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the publisher's offer made in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was the offer to make amends made in time` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The publisher has made me an offer to make amends: does it contain what the Act requires: in writing, identifiable as such, a correction, steps to tell others, my expenses, and any limit stated (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 15(1)(a)-(f))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has made you an offer to make amends for the matter
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the publisher's offer a proper offer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The publisher has made me an offer to make amends: if I accept it, can I still sue (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 17(1): not once the publisher has carried it out)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has made you an offer to make amends for the matter
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
      `the publisher has carried out its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has done everything the accepted offer promised, including paying any compensation
GIVETH AN `If the offer is accepted`
`What follows if I accept the offer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends`
        THEN `the acceptance answer` (`What happens if I accept the offer` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`) (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`) `the publisher has carried out its terms`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The publisher has made me an offer to make amends: if I refuse it, does the publisher get a defence (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 18(1): if the court finds the offer prompt, backed by readiness, and reasonable)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has made you an offer to make amends for the matter
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
      `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher offered as soon as practicable after learning the matter is or may be defamatory
      `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher stood ready, before trial, to carry out the offer
      `the court finds the offer was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the offer reasonable in all the circumstances (s 18(2) lists what it weighs)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does refusing the offer give the publisher a defence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN
        IF `the publisher has made me an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my refusal give the publisher a defence` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`) (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`) `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable` `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out` `the court finds the offer was reasonable`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person defamed and the publisher: defences and damages`

§§§ `ss 25, 26, 31, 33 -- truth, honest opinion and triviality`

@export Which of the defences of truth, contextual truth, honest opinion or triviality answers the claim (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 25, 26, 31, 33; privilege, fair report and innocent dissemination are not covered)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the imputations complained of are substantially true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the defamatory imputations complained of substantially true (s 25)
      `other imputations in the matter are substantially true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds other imputations carried by the matter (contextual imputations) substantially true (s 26)
      `the imputations complained of do no further harm because of those` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the imputations complained of do no further harm to the reputation, because of the truth of the contextual imputations (s 26)
      `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter was an expression of the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact (s 31(1)(a))
      `the opinion related to a matter of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the opinion related to a matter of public interest (s 31(1)(b))
      `the opinion is based on proper material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the opinion is based on proper material: substantially true, or published on a privileged occasion or under a defence in s 28, 29 or 31 (s 31(1)(c), (5))
      `the person defamed proves the opinion was not honestly held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed proves the publisher did not honestly hold the opinion when it was published (s 31(4)(a))
      `the person defamed was unlikely to sustain any harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the circumstances of publication were such that the person defamed was unlikely to sustain any harm (s 33)
GIVETH A `Which defence`
`Which defence answers the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN `the defence answer` (`Which defence defeats my claim` (`the findings from` `the imputations complained of are substantially true` `other imputations in the matter are substantially true` `the imputations complained of do no further harm because of those` `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact` `the opinion related to a matter of public interest` `the opinion is based on proper material` `the person defamed proves the opinion was not honestly held` `the person defamed was unlikely to sustain any harm`))
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN `the defence answer` (`Which defence defeats my claim` (`the findings from` `the imputations complained of are substantially true` `other imputations in the matter are substantially true` `the imputations complained of do no further harm because of those` `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact` `the opinion related to a matter of public interest` `the opinion is based on proper material` `the person defamed proves the opinion was not honestly held` `the person defamed was unlikely to sustain any harm`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35, 37 -- damages`

@export What will the next maximum damages amount for non-economic loss be: the last amount adjusted by average weekly earnings, rounded to the nearest $500 (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 35(4), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amount last applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount currently applicable ($250,000 if none has been declared)
      `the percentage change in average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The Statistician's percentage change in average weekly total earnings of full-time adults over the 4 quarters, e.g. 3.5 for 3.5%
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the next damages cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN amount (`What will the next maximum damages amount be` `the amount last applicable` `the percentage change in average weekly earnings`)
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN amount (`What will the next maximum damages amount be` `the amount last applicable` `the percentage change in average weekly earnings`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most that can be awarded for non-economic loss: the court's assessment, capped at the maximum damages amount unless aggravated damages are warranted (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 35(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `damages assessed for non-economic loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of damages for non-economic loss (hurt to reputation and feelings), in dollars
      `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied the circumstances of publication warrant aggravated damages (s 35(2))
      `the maximum damages amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount applicable when damages are awarded (the Minister's latest Gazette order; $250,000 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most for non-economic loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN amount (`How much can I get for non-economic loss` (`the assessment from` 0 `damages assessed for non-economic loss` 0 `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`) `the maximum damages amount`)
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN amount (`How much can I get for non-economic loss` (`the assessment from` 0 `damages assessed for non-economic loss` 0 `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`) `the maximum damages amount`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 37: no exemplary or punitive damages, so what is sought as such is not an input (the baseline's field is 0).
@export How much can be awarded in damages in all: economic loss in full, non-economic loss within the cap, and no exemplary or punitive damages (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 35, 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `damages assessed for economic loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of damages for economic loss (lost income or business), in dollars
      `damages assessed for non-economic loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of damages for non-economic loss (hurt to reputation and feelings), in dollars
      `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied the circumstances of publication warrant aggravated damages (s 35(2))
      `the maximum damages amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount applicable when damages are awarded (the Minister's latest Gazette order; $250,000 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What can be awarded in all` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I, or my company, have been defamed, or say so` THEN amount (`How much can I be awarded in all` (`the assessment from` `damages assessed for economic loss` `damages assessed for non-economic loss` 0 `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`) `the maximum damages amount`)
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN amount (`How much can I be awarded in all` (`the assessment from` `damages assessed for economic loss` `damages assessed for non-economic loss` 0 `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`) `the maximum damages amount`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the publisher`

§§§ `ss 7-10, 23; Limitation Act ss 15, 40 -- can they sue me, and by when`

@export The matter is about a company: is it an "excluded corporation", one that may sue me: a not-for-profit, or a company with fewer than 10 full-time-equivalent employees not related to another, and not a public body (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 9(2)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who the matter is about` IS A `Who the matter is about` @desc Who the matter you published is about: a living person, a company, or a person who has died
      `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the objects for which the company is formed include obtaining financial gain for its members (that is, it is for profit)
      `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the company employed when the matter was published, counting part-timers as fractions of a full-time equivalent
      `the company is related to another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is related to another corporation (Corporations Act 2001 s 50: a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary)
      `the company is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is a local government body or other governmental or public authority
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the company sue me for defamation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `it is about a company` `who the matter is about`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my company an excluded corporation` (`the company from` `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` `the company is related to another corporation` `the company is a public body`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The publisher asking is alive, so s 10(b) (a publisher who has died) is FALSE by the role's own terms.
@export Can they sue me for defamation over what I published: no loss need be shown, but not over a person who has died (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 7-10, 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who the matter is about` IS A `Who the matter is about` @desc Who the matter you published is about: a living person, a company, or a person who has died
      `the matter carries a defamatory imputation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter carries an imputation that is defamatory of the person or company it is about (the general law decides what is defamatory)
      `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the objects for which the company is formed include obtaining financial gain for its members (that is, it is for profit)
      `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the company employed when the matter was published, counting part-timers as fractions of a full-time equivalent
      `the company is related to another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is related to another corporation (Corporations Act 2001 s 50: a holding company, subsidiary or fellow subsidiary)
      `the company is a public body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is a local government body or other governmental or public authority
      `the publisher has already been sued for damages over this or like matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed has already sued this publisher for damages over this matter, or like matter
      `the court has given leave for the further proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave for the further proceedings (s 23)
GIVETH A `Whether there is a claim`
`Can they sue me over what I published` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN `the claim answer` (`May I sue for defamation` (`the publication from` (`the baseline's whose reputation for` `who the matter is about`) `the matter carries a defamatory imputation` (`the company from` `the company's objects include obtaining financial gain for its members` `the company's full-time-equivalent employees` `the company is related to another corporation` `the company is a public body`) FALSE `the publisher has already been sued for damages over this or like matter` `the court has given leave for the further proceedings`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Are they still in time to sue me: one year from publication, or up to 3 if the court extends it (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 15, 40)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `full months since publication` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since the matter was published
      `the court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already extended the time to sue under Limitation Act s 40
GIVETH A `The time to sue`
`Is there still time to sue me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN `the time answer` (`Am I in time to sue` `full months since publication` `the court has extended the time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 14 -- a concerns notice sent to me`

@export I have been sent a notice about the matter: is it a "concerns notice", in writing and naming the imputations, with any further particulars I asked for given within 14 days (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 14(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a notice about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who says they are defamed has sent or given you a notice (a letter, an email, a message) about the matter
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is in writing
      `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice tells the publisher the defamatory imputations the person defamed says the matter carries about them
      `the publisher asked for further particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher gave a further particulars notice, asking for more detail of the imputations
      `days taken to give the further particulars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days were taken to give them (a large number if they were never given)
      `extra days the publisher agreed to` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 the publisher agreed to for the further particulars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the notice sent to me a concerns notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have been sent a notice about the matter`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my notice a concerns notice` (`the notice from` `the notice is in writing` `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` `the publisher asked for further particulars` `days taken to give the further particulars` `extra days the publisher agreed to`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have been sent a notice about the matter: what does it do (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 14(1)(a): a concerns notice starts my 28 days to offer to make amends)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a notice about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who says they are defamed has sent or given you a notice (a letter, an email, a message) about the matter
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is in writing
      `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice tells the publisher the defamatory imputations the person defamed says the matter carries about them
      `the publisher asked for further particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher gave a further particulars notice, asking for more detail of the imputations
      `days taken to give the further particulars` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days were taken to give them (a large number if they were never given)
      `extra days the publisher agreed to` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 the publisher agreed to for the further particulars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `What the notice does`
`What does the notice sent to me do` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have been sent a notice about the matter`
        THEN `the notice answer` (`What does my notice do` (`the notice from` `the notice is in writing` `the notice names the defamatory imputations said to be carried` `the publisher asked for further particulars` `days taken to give the further particulars` `extra days the publisher agreed to`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14-18 -- my offer to make amends`

@export I am making an offer to make amends: may I still make it, within 28 days of the concerns notice and before I serve a defence, or as a genuine renewal within 14 days of withdrawing (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) ss 14(1), 16(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or are about to make, an offer to make amends to the person who says they are defamed
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I still make an offer to make amends` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was the offer to make amends made in time` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am making an offer to make amends: does it contain what the Act requires: in writing, identifiable as such, a correction, steps to tell others, the other side's expenses, and any limit stated (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 15(1)(a)-(f))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or are about to make, an offer to make amends to the person who says they are defamed
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my offer to make amends a proper offer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have made an offer to make amends: if it is accepted and I carry it out, can they still sue me (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 17(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or are about to make, an offer to make amends to the person who says they are defamed
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
      `the publisher has carried out its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has done everything the accepted offer promised, including paying any compensation
GIVETH AN `If the offer is accepted`
`What follows if my offer is accepted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends`
        THEN `the acceptance answer` (`What happens if I accept the offer` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`) (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`) `the publisher has carried out its terms`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have made an offer to make amends: if it is refused, do I have a defence (Defamation Act 2005 (WA) s 18(1): if the court finds I made it as soon as practicable, stood ready to carry it out, and it was reasonable)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or are about to make, an offer to make amends to the person who says they are defamed
      `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person defamed gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `days from the concerns notice to the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the concerns notice to the offer
      `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher had served a defence in an action over the matter before the offer
      `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer renews, in different terms, an offer the publisher withdrew
      `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the renewed offer is a genuine attempt to address the concerns raised about the withdrawn offer
      `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer
      `days for renewal agreed beyond 14` IS A NUMBER @desc Any days beyond 14 agreed for the renewed offer (0 if none)
      `the offer is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is in writing
      `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act
      `it is limited to particular imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer is limited to particular defamatory imputations
      `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If limited: whether it says so and particularises the imputations
      `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable correction
      `the publisher gave the material to others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher (or someone with its knowledge) gave material containing the matter to others
      `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether it offers to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell them the matter is or may be defamatory
      `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it offers to pay the expenses the person defamed reasonably incurred before the offer and in considering it
      `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher offered as soon as practicable after learning the matter is or may be defamatory
      `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher stood ready, before trial, to carry out the offer
      `the court finds the offer was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the offer reasonable in all the circumstances (s 18(2) lists what it weighs)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a refusal of my offer give me a defence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I published something that someone says defames them` THEN
        IF `I have made, or am making, an offer to make amends`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my refusal give the publisher a defence` (`the timing from` `a concerns notice was given to the publisher` `days from the concerns notice to the offer` `the publisher had served a defence before the offer` `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms` `it is a genuine attempt to meet the concerns about the withdrawn offer` `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` `days for renewal agreed beyond 14`) (`the offer from` `the offer is in writing` `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act` `it is limited to particular imputations` `it states the limit and particularises those imputations` `it offers to publish a reasonable correction` `the publisher gave the material to others` `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others` `it offers to pay the reasonable expenses of the person defamed`) `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable` `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out` `the court finds the offer was reasonable`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
